                      "id":  "vibeguard",
                      "title":  "vibeguard — AI Code Guard",
                      "description":  "The AI code reality check. A zero-dependency pre-commit guard with 10 deterministic rules, plus a browser-based AI Studio that hunts bugs and vulnerabilities.",
                      "longDescription":  "vibeguard is a pre-commit guard for your terminal plus a browser-based AI Studio — without ever uploading your keys or your code. The CLI uses ten deterministic rules tuned for what LLMs repeat most: empty catch blocks that swallow errors, null derefs from .find() and JSON.parse(), invented env vars, hardcoded API keys, and sleep-hack \u0027fixes\u0027 that hide races. Errors block the commit with a red exit code; warnings are logged and watched. The AI Studio layers an optional deep dive on top — seven modes (bug finder, security audit, fix \u0026 explain, API \u0026 deployment, full audit report, and Website Scanner, which takes any live URL and audits the grabbed page for web vulnerabilities) with a Risk Score /100 and line-level fixes. It ships with eight free-tier providers (Gemini, Groq, OpenRouter, Cerebras, Mistral, GitHub Models, NVIDIA NIM, plus custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints), takes input by paste, file upload, live GitHub repo fetch, or live website scan, downloads reports as Markdown, HTML, or JSON, and stores API keys only in your browser\u0027s localStorage behind a stateless relay.",
